  "lines": [
    {
      "start": 0.45,
      "dur": 2.67,
      "text": "What Would It Take to Say We Found Life?"
    },
    {
      "start": 3.91,
      "dur": 2.6,
      "text": "We Asked a NASA Scientist."
    },
    {
      "start": 6.63,
      "dur": 1.97,
      "text": "We call this the podium test."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.6,
      "dur": 0.67,
      "text": "What would it take"
    },
    {
      "start": 9.27,
      "dur": 0.4,
      "text": "for you"
    },
    {
      "start": 9.67,
      "dur": 1.8,
      "text": "personally to confidently stand up"
    },
    {
      "start": 11.47,
      "dur": 1.6,
      "text": "in front of an international audience"
    },
    {
      "start": 13.07,
      "dur": 1.37,
      "text": "and make that claim?"
    },
    {
      "start": 14.43,
      "dur": 1.3,
      "text": "When you put it in that way,"
    },
    {
      "start": 15.73,
      "dur": 1.63,
      "text": "I think for a lot of scientists,"
    },
    {
      "start": 17.37,
      "dur": 1.77,
      "text": "the bar is really high."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.13,
      "dur": 0.53,
      "text": "So of course,"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.67,
      "dur": 1.17,
      "text": "there would be obvious things,"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.83,
      "dur": 0.9,
      "text": "you know, a very clear"
    },
    {
      "start": 21.73,
      "dur": 1.23,
      "text": "signature of technology"
    },
    {
      "start": 22.97,
      "dur": 2.3,
      "text": "or a skeleton or something like that."
    },
    {
      "start": 25.27,
      "dur": 1.4,
      "text": "But we think that a lot of the evidence"
    },
    {
      "start": 26.67,
      "dur": 0.93,
      "text": "that we might encounter"
    },
    {
      "start": 27.6,
      "dur": 1.5,
      "text": "first will be much more subtle."
    },
    {
      "start": 29.1,
      "dur": 1.83,
      "text": "For example, chemical signs of life"
    },
    {
      "start": 30.93,
      "dur": 1.0,
      "text": "that have to be"
    },
    {
      "start": 31.93,
      "dur": 1.5,
      "text": "detected above a background"
    },
    {
      "start": 33.44,
      "dur": 1.97,
      "text": "of abiotic chemistry."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.4,
      "dur": 1.07,
      "text": "And really, what we see"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.47,
      "dur": 2.13,
      "text": "might depend a lot on where we look."
    },
    {
      "start": 38.6,
      "dur": 1.7,
      "text": "On Mars, for example,"
    },
    {
      "start": 40.3,
      "dur": 1.53,
      "text": "the long history of exploration"
    },
    {
      "start": 41.84,
      "dur": 1.5,
      "text": "there gives us a lot of context"
    },
    {
      "start": 43.34,
      "dur": 1.43,
      "text": "for what we might find."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.77,
      "dur": 0.67,
      "text": "But we're potentially"
    },
    {
      "start": 45.44,
      "dur": 0.97,
      "text": "talking about samples"
    },
    {
      "start": 46.4,
      "dur": 1.37,
      "text": "that are billions of years old"
    },
    {
      "start": 47.77,
      "dur": 1.7,
      "text": "in those cases, and on Earth,"
    },
    {
      "start": 49.47,
      "dur": 1.1,
      "text": "those kinds of samples,"
    },
    {
      "start": 50.57,
      "dur": 1.3,
      "text": "the evidence of life is often"
    },
    {
      "start": 51.87,
      "dur": 2.27,
      "text": "degraded and difficult to detect."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.14,
      "dur": 0.9,
      "text": "On the ocean worlds"
    },
    {
      "start": 55.04,
      "dur": 1.13,
      "text": "of our outer solar system,"
    },
    {
      "start": 56.17,
      "dur": 2.93,
      "text": "so places like Jupiter's moon Europa"
    },
    {
      "start": 59.1,
      "dur": 1.83,
      "text": "and Saturn's moon Enceladus,"
    },
    {
      "start": 60.94,
      "dur": 0.83,
      "text": "there's the tantalizing"
    },
    {
      "start": 61.77,
